%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% Scenario: interleaved by row, the image taller than the mask. A 4x4
% grey image under a 4x2 mask with Decode [0 1]: each block is one
% mask row then two image rows, so each mask row governs the two image
% rows of its block. The mask keeps the outer columns of the upper half
% and the inner columns of the lower half off the page.
/backdrop {
  0.3 setgray 0 0 1 1 rectfill
  0 setgray 0 0.25 0.75 { 0 0.125 1 rectfill } for
} def
gsave
100 400 translate 200 200 scale
backdrop
%%BeginData: 8 ASCII Lines
<< /ImageType 3 /InterleaveType 2
   /DataDict << /ImageType 1 /Width 4 /Height 4 /BitsPerComponent 8
      /ImageMatrix [4 0 0 -4 0 4] /Decode [0 1]
      /DataSource currentfile /ASCIIHexDecode filter >>
   /MaskDict << /ImageType 1 /Width 4 /Height 2 /BitsPerComponent 1
      /ImageMatrix [4 0 0 -2 0 2] /Decode [0 1] >> >> image
90 FFFFFFFF E0E0E0E0
60 C0C0C0C0 A0A0A0A0 >
%%EndData
grestore
0 setgray 4 setlinewidth
100 380 moveto 300 380 lineto stroke
showpage
